    "result_text": "All 11 tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS), including the new `Cp05Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a created owner expose a `displayName` field formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`. The acceptance test creates an owner and reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, asserting `$.displayName == \"LastName, FirstName\"`, so the field had to appear on the `OwnerDto` returned by the response mapper.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the code-generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` computing `displayName` from the stored entity names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause the value is derived in the mapper from the persisted `lastName`/`firstName`, it's computed from the stored names (not the raw request) and is consistent across both the create response and subsequent GETs \u2014 no new OfficeFloor pipeline step was needed since the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated`/`RespondWithOwner` functions already run everything through `OwnerMapper`.",
